.el .ds Aq '
.TH geectl-build-wipe-binaries 1  "geectl-build-wipe-binaries 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-wipe\-binaries \- Wipe the binary packages of a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the wipe. At least one scope selector is required: `\-\-all`, `\-\-arch`, `\-\-repository`, or a status filter
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build wipe\-binaries\fR [\fB\-\-arch\fR] [\fB\-\-repository\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-build\-disabled\fR] [\fB\-\-build\-failed\fR] [\fB\-\-broken\fR] [\fB\-\-unresolvable\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> [\fIPACKAGE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wipe the binary packages of a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the wipe. At least one scope selector is required: `\-\-all`, `\-\-arch`, `\-\-repository`, or a status filter
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-arch\fR \fI<ARCH>\fR
Wipe only binaries for this architecture
.TP
\fB\-\-repository\fR \fI<REPOSITORY>\fR
Wipe only binaries for this repository
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Wipe all binaries regardless of package status. Combines with no status filter
.TP
\fB\-\-build\-disabled\fR
Wipe only binaries of packages whose build is disabled
.TP
\fB\-\-build\-failed\fR
Wipe only binaries of packages whose build failed
.TP
\fB\-\-broken\fR
Wipe only binaries of packages whose sources are bad
.TP
\fB\-\-unresolvable\fR
Wipe only binaries of packages with dependency errors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to wipe binaries in
.TP
[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
The package to wipe binaries for. Omit to wipe the whole project
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
